      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "LIYAH'S GIRL (1) produced a sharp finish to win her maiden in style at Newcastle in August, and she could have won either of her net 2 starts at Canberra had she made a better beginning, finishing runner-up in each of those efforts. She carries 3kg less here, and can go one better. GOSH ALMIGHTY (9) settled a long way back from a wide draw at Kembla Grange 12 days ago, and unwound strongly to finish second by a length over 2000m. He can race a lot closer to the pace from a superior gate this time, and will be among the hardest to hold out here. WIZARD'S STAR (7) has been racing well enough at provincial level without winning, and he drops into a very winnable race here. Stick with him on an each-way basis. KOJAK (4) found the drop back to 1400m too much for him when finishing out of the money at Dubbo 11 days ago, but that run would have cleaned him up nicely for this more suitable assignment over 2100m. Don't drop him. DENISE'S GAL (8) is an honest mare with top 4 claims as well.",
